WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.870
-My first guest is
an Oscar, Golden Globe,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.305
and seven-time Emmy winner,

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.574
starring on
the hit comedy series "Mom,"

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:11.210
which is airing its
eighth and final season

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.047
Thursdays at 9:00 p.m. on CBS.

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.416
Here is Allison Janney!

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.883
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:20.085
Oh!

00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:24.791
Oh, I'm so happy you're here.
Allison Janney!

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.992
You look fantastic.
-Jimmy --

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.160
-Thank you.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.463
-Jimmy, I can't --
I mean, I cannot believe

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.165
that I'm finally
meeting you this way.

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:36.402
But this is the first time
I'm doing your show.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:39.071
And I just want to ask you
why have you taken so long

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.641
to ask for me to be here?

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.309
-That sounds so bizarre to me.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:47.213
I feel like we've had
great interviews.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.681
-We have?

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.449
-Haven't we?

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.485
-No, we haven't.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.854
-This is our
first interview together.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.090
-Oh, well, this is
going to be memorable.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.227
-I'm a virgin,
so be kind and gentle.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.996
-We'll never forget this day --
April 14th.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.499
4-1-4...
-4-1-4 is our date.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.468
-...will forever be
in our hearts.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.769
-I love you.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.271
-I love you. I'm a big fan.
And you're fantastic.

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.641
I want to get into
so many things.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.642
But let's talk about "Mom."

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:20.245
You wrapped up,
finished filming.

00:01:20.245 --> 00:01:21.647
This is eight seasons.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:25.184
This is 170 episodes.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.520
It's got to be emotional.
Is it bittersweet?

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.023
What is it?
-You know what? It's everything.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.590
As everything is,
it's never one thing.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.226
Sometimes, I'd be
driving on the lot,

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.628
and it was like, "Oh, my God.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.130
This is the last Monday I'll be

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.497
driving on
the Warner Bros. lot."

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:39.632
And I was filming myself.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.666
And, of course, that one day,

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.168
it was a guard
who didn't know me.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.336
So it was like, you know,
"Can I see your I.D.?"

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.605
And I was like, "It's me!"

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:48.741
You know, and, no,
he didn't know who I was.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.376
But then I'd come on,

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.877
and just everything
would make me cry.

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.979
And then, the next day,
I'd come on and feel like,

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:56.148
"I'm so excited this is ending.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.583
I get a new chapter of life."

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.952
It was the biggest, you know,

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:01.587
emotional roller-coaster ride.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.290
And, sometimes, people would be
sobbing, and I'd feel nothing.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.290
And I'd be like,
"What's wrong with me?

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.425
What's wrong with me?"

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:07.860
And then the
next -- You know, it was --

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.229
Literally everyone
was all over the place.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.398
And it was really sad.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:16.201
We all -- It was such a family
we had there, so we're sad.

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:19.138
We're sad we're not coming back
to tell more of these stories,

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:20.539
'cause I think
it's so important.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:22.775
And, you know, it's so great
when you get to entertain people

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.777
but also put something
out there in the world

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:28.047
that helps destigmatize
something like recovery

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.783
and make it
more approachable to people.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.952
And it's done so much
for so many people.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:36.321
It just -- I get tons of letters
and fans coming up to me

00:02:36.321 --> 00:02:38.624
so appreciative of what
the show has done for them.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.293
-Yeah! Thank you for
doing that, by the way.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.294
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:45.632
It is -- it is -- it is great
when you can do both.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.100
Did you steal
any props or anything?

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.035
-Well, just between
you and me...

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:53.172
-Yeah, no one's watching.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.642
-I did -- I had to --
It's funny,

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:58.178
because no one knew I was
wearing a wig.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.679
And I come in for
this season of "Mom,"

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:02.715
and the producers
see me like this.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.783
And they're like,
"What have you done?!

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:07.053
How are we going to do --

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.522
You should have asked us before
you did this to your hair."

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.724
And I'm like, "Guys, I've been
wearing a wig since Season 1."

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.592
But nobody knew it.

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:15.094
So, everybody in the world
knows it now.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.797
But -- So, that wig
is coming with me.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:20.332
And a few pairs of sweatpants,
'cause my character, Bonnie,

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:21.534
loved to be comfortable,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.902
as does Allison Janney.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:27.106
So I took a lot of those --
a lot of sweatpants.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.576
-You were -- Do you know what
you're going to do next?

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.078
'Cause you've done theater and
you knocked it out of the park.

00:03:33.078 --> 00:03:34.747
You've done movies.
You knocked it out of the park.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.915
You do drama, you knock it --

00:03:36.915 --> 00:03:38.584
Sitcom, knock it
out of the park.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.453
What's next for you?

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:43.656
-Well, I decided to,
as I like to do all the time,

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.725
whatever I've done --
the last thing I've done,

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.194
I like to shake it up and do
something completely different.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:52.265
So I've decided, Jimmy,
that I'm going to go do

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:55.835
an action-thriller movie,
and I'm about to start training

00:03:55.835 --> 00:04:00.205
with a fight trainer
two hours a day

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:02.742
and learn to fight to kill

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.244
and to be a bad-ass,
like, you know,

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:09.215
female Dirty Harry
in this movie called "Lou"

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.316
that I'm about to start filming.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.318
-Wow! Already,
the audience is into it.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.053
[ Cheers and applause ]
I want to see this.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.822
This is fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:18.891
Say a prayer that
I survive it, you know,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.626
'cause it's going to be --
It'll be pretty cool.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:22.995
-Oh, you're going to be great!
-I hope so.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.564
-Can I quickly ask?

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:28.934
The sleeping dog behind you --
what's its name?

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.303
-Yes. Well, that's Dutch.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:32.871
And Dutch is my protector.

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:35.140
And he's very interested in
our interview, you can see.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.409
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.844
He looks like one of
those protective dogs, yeah.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:38.844
-Oh, he is.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:40.879
He actually --
He's a cattle dog,

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:44.716
so he likes to nip at people's
heels, which is not --

00:04:44.716 --> 00:04:46.985
You know, most guests
who come into my house,

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:51.257
I give them ankle guards
so they don't get bit by Dutch.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.825
But he is a sweetheart.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.028
-Well, he is also making his
debut on "The Tonight Show,"

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.662
so this really will be
a memorable --

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:57.796
I knew this interview
would be memorable.

00:04:57.796 --> 00:04:59.031
It's you and Dutch.

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.667
-I wish the other dogs
would come here, but --

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.603
I got two more around here
somewhere, but they're shy.

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:07.807
-Allison, congrats on the
success of "Mom" and everything.

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.875
And please come on
the show more often.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.043
I'd like to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:12.411
Here's Allison Janney in

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:14.447
tomorrow night's episode
of "Mom."

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:15.581
Take a look.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.949
-What you got going on there?

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.251
-Oh, I need to hold on to
the lumber

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.519
when I make a turn,
and I got a splinter.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.587
I'm gonna start wearing
gloves when I drive.

00:05:22.587 --> 00:05:24.023
-That's your solution?

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:27.359
-Yeah, mittens would make it
too hard to change the radio.

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:30.563
-Or perhaps the time
has come to buy a truck.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.064
-Oh, she can't afford a truck.

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.000
-Whoa! Bonnie just said what
the voice in my head

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.135
said at the exact same time.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.670
-That means my voice
is in your head.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.405
That's a good thing.
That saves lives.

00:05:40.405 --> 00:05:41.774
-I bet you can afford it.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.976
You're very cheap --
I-I mean, frugal.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.578
-I'm not sure I'm ready.

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:48.614
-I miss my red socks.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.483
-Are you okay?
Is she having a stroke?

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:52.652
Do you smell toast?

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.186
Wait. I smell toast.
Am I having a stroke?

00:05:54.186 --> 00:05:57.756
No, we're in a diner.
Carry on.

00:05:57.756 --> 00:06:01.093
-Yeah. I love it.
Allison Janney, everybody!

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:06.366
Catch the final season of "Mom"
Thursdays at 9:00 p.m. on CBS.

